@cebe All examples are fictitious. I have no claim to all but the last example 
(with `['AND' , [], 'string']`)

@qiangxue Ok, it is necessary to describe in comments here - http://www.yiiframework.com/doc-2.0/yii-db-baseactiverecord.html#findOne()-detail
And now there is:

``` php
// find the first customer whose age is 30 and whose status is 1
$customer = Customer::findOne(['age' => 30, 'status' => 1]);
// the above code is equivalent to:
$customer = Customer::find()->where(['age' => 30, 'status' => 1])->one();
//....
```

"equivalent" makes it clear that everything is the same.
